Z||000003||CoolBlue87GT||10-28-2001||10:12 PM||||Steering improved - tighter turning.<BR>Front wheels have smaller "lip"<BR>Handle better<P>There's many more things. Just the first things I thought of.||||reg||6
Z||000004||Nashco||10-28-2001||10:37 PM||||I don't know of any links right off hand, but here are the differences I know for sure:<P>Redesigned front suspension (completely redesigned..not a thing or two)<BR>88 V6 gets better engine oiling properties<BR>88 2.5 gets distrubutorless ignition system (DIS)<BR>Redesigned rear suspension (completely redesigned...the "best" change in 88)<BR>Interior color options changed (Beachwood is an 88 only color)<BR>Interior seating options changed (Cloth seats with lumbar adjustment and Leather seats available)(not positive this is 88 only)<BR>Brakes changed from solid to vented rotor design.<BR>Exhaust is different as a result of rear cradle changes<BR>Front wheels have less diameter (thus different offset) as a result of front suspension redesign<BR>Factory option for t-tops<P>That's all I can come up with now...I'm sure there's more.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||10-29-2001||09:20 AM||||hmmm...my post never showed up. if you've got a loaal library nearby with road and track back issues there's a fall '87 issue (forgot which month) where they review the '88 and describe the changes. or it could be reprinted somewhere on the net. in fact i'm almost sure i've seen it on the net somewhere. it was a comparision review with an mr2 and maybe a crx too.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||10-29-2001||09:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>I don't know of any links right off hand, but here are the differences I know for sure:<P>Redesigned front suspension (completely redesigned..not a thing or two)<BR>88 V6 gets better engine oiling properties<BR>88 2.5 gets distrubutorless ignition system (DIS)<BR>Redesigned rear suspension (completely redesigned...the "best" change in 88)<BR>Interior color options changed (Beachwood is an 88 only color)<BR>Interior seating options changed (Cloth seats with lumbar adjustment and Leather seats available)(not positive this is 88 only)<BR>Brakes changed from solid to vented rotor design.<BR>Exhaust is different as a result of rear cradle changes<BR>Front wheels have less diameter (thus different offset) as a result of front suspension redesign<BR>Factory option for t-tops<P>That's all I can come up with now...I'm sure there's more.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>2.5L went to DIS ignition in 1987.<BR>1988 V-6 is also internally balanced.<BR>The only part of the exhaust that changed was the "Y" pipe. The rest of the exhaust is the same. The cradle has nothing to do with the exhaust change.<BR>Rear suspension gets a sway bar on Formula and GT.<BR>Front wheels have different width not diameter. But this is only on the 15" lace wheels not the 13" or 14" wheels.<P>Monochrome paint on GT's (No silver trim on bottom)<BR>Yellow is an 88 color only.<BR>On V-6 cars the cooling tubes and blower motor in trunk were removed.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Nashco||10-29-2001||08:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B> 2.5L went to DIS ignition in 1987.<BR>1988 V-6 is also internally balanced.<BR>The only part of the exhaust that changed was the "Y" pipe. The rest of the exhaust is the same. The cradle has nothing to do with the exhaust change.<BR>Rear suspension gets a sway bar on Formula and GT.<BR>Front wheels have different width not diameter. But this is only on the 15" lace wheels not the 13" or 14" wheels.<P>Monochrome paint on GT's (No silver trim on bottom)<BR>Yellow is an 88 color only.<BR>On V-6 cars the cooling tubes and blower motor in trunk were removed.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>HA!  Wow, good call Oreif, I blew it!  Some of those were just stupid mistakes, but thanks for the additional info <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I forgot about a couple of those.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>||||reg||1
